.TITLE "chmod"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Changes file modes or Access Control Lists (ACLs). It manages the __permissions__ of files and directories to control who can read, write, or execute them.

.DIV "TLDR"
**chmod 755 file.txt**
Sets specific octal permissions for a file.
> __755__ octal mode | __file.txt__ target file

**chmod +x script.sh**
Adds execute permission to a specific file.
> __+x__ execute permission | __script.sh__ target script

**chmod -R 777 directory/**
Changes permissions for a directory and all its contents recursively.
> __-R__ recursive flag | __777__ permissive mode | __directory/__ target folder

**chmod u+w file.txt**
Adds write permission for the owner of the file.
> __u+w__ user write permission

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Properly managing permissions with __chmod__ is critical for system security. Always use the most restrictive permissions necessary for a file or application to function.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:chown** **mac:ls**

